            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibred+product"} fibred product
            over
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_57.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            of the coequaliser diagram. Since
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_58.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \setminus \{0\}
            has no points mapping to
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_59.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_60.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mi Y
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R} \setminus \{0\}) \times_{\mathbb{R}} Y = \emptyset
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_61.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ⨿
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mi Y
                    %mo =
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ⨿
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R} \amalg \mathbb{R}) \times_{\mathbb{R}} Y = Y \amalg Y
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_62.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ⨿
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \to Y \amalg Y
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_63.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ⨿
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \amalg Y
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_64.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ⨿
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \amalg Y
            are of the form
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_65.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i, \beta)
            where
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_66.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            is a constant in
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_67.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,*\}
            that distinguishes the cofactors and
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_68.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta : \mathbb{R} \to Y
            is a smooth curve in
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_69.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %p
            Let us consider the product over
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_70.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            of
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_71.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \cup \{*\}
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_72.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_73.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ⨿
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \amalg Y
            again. However, as a Frölicher space it has different functions to those on
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_74.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ⨿
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \amalg Y
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_75.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            is a subspace of
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_76.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R} \cup \{*\}) \times Y
            and thus a curve into it is smooth if and only if it is smooth into
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_77.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R} \cup \{*\}) \times Y
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_78.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \cup \{*\}
            and to
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_79.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are smooth. As we are considering curves in
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_80.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R} \cup \{*\}) \times_\mathbb{R} Y
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_81.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \cup \{*\}
            must have image in
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_82.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,*\}
            %em any
            curve is allowed by this and so the smooth curves into
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_83.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℝ
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R} \cup \{*\}) \times_\mathbb{R} Y
            are of the form
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_84.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi α
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\alpha, \beta)
            where
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_85.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            is
            %em any
            function from
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_86.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            into
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_87.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,*\}
            and
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_88.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta : \mathbb{R} \to Y
            is a smooth curve in
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_89.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          .query
            %p
              I notice that in some classically false versions of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_90.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              to
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_91.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,*\}
              are the constant ones. It would be nice if there were a nonclassical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dream+mathematics"} dream universe
              in which the category of Frölicher spaces were locally cartesian closed! Unfortunately, the counterexample can be saved by using a continuously parametrised coproduct
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_92.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{\mathbb{R}} \mathbb{R}
              instead of
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_93.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ⨿
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{\{0,*\}} \mathbb{R} = \mathbb{R} \amalg \mathbb{R}
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Stacey"} Andrew Stacey
              I think I’d be disappointed if locally cartesian became a property of what set theory was being used! I suspect that the real reason this example works is the fact that
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_94.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to \mathbb{R}
              has such bad path-lifting properties and the coequaliser diagram that I chose is just a simple one that demonstrates it.
            %p I’ve been pondering how one might fix this. I ought to write up Kriegl and Michor’s extension of a manifold as, although they haven’t done much with it, it contains some ideas that may be of interest. What makes me think of it here is that that definition of a manifold (which isn’t, by the way, the one in their weighty tome) has two parts: a space and its tangent space, and relationships between them. This suggests that a smooth space, of whatever variety, should be more than just one space but some sort of diagram of spaces.
            %p
              This is also suggested by trying to generalise the Frolicher “idea” to non-set-based theories. It’s not immediately obvious how to make the saturation condition work, but the basic idea is to have objects as
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_95.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,F,c)
              with
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_96.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi Hom
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c : C \times F \to Hom
              and morphisms as
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_97.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi Hom
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C_X \times F_Y \to Hom
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_98.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              needs some sort of saturation condition as well as a compatibility condition.
          %p
            This is not the same as
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_99.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \coprod Y
            and thus the functor
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_100.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℝ
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - \times_{\mathbb{R}} Y
            does not preserve colimits. It cannot, therefore, be a left adjoint and so the category of Frölicher spaces is not locally cartesian closed.
          %p
            This example works because of the structure of
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_101.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \cup \{*\}
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_102.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \cup \{*\}
            would be determined by those curves which lift to
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_103.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \coprod \mathbb{R}
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_104.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            and
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_105.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
            because up in
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_106.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \coprod \mathbb{R}
            these two points are far apart. Thus the subspace structure on
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_107.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,*\}
            in an “input only” category is
            = succeed "." do
              %em discrete
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_108.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \cup \{*\}
            cannot detect the difference between
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_109.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_110.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_111.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \cup \{*\}
            are allowed to swap between them with aplomb. The subspace structure on
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_112.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,*\}
            is thus the
            %em indiscrete
            structure.
          %p
            Working in the category of
            %em Hausdorff
            Frölicher spaces (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#hausdorff"} below
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_113.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \coprod Y
            as before but taking the coequaliser and then the product yields just
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_114.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %p
            It is also worth pointing out that with the modification of the previous paragraph, this example only involves manifolds (assuming that
            %math#mathml_aa4aa9075830b6d749d1c29a560732ae809d1b7b_115.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is chosen to be a manifold). It therefore shows that a category extending that of smooth manifolds can
            %strong either
            be locally cartesian closed
            %strong or
            preserve limits and colimits from manifolds
            = succeed "." do
              %em but not both
